message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "EDI: Experimental Design and Inference"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-10"
authors:
  - family-names: Kapelner
    given-names: Adam
    email: kapelner@qc.cuny.edu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5985-6792"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kapelner/EDI"
url: "https://github.com/kapelner/EDI"
license: GPL-3.0
keywords:
  - experimental design
  - covariate balance
  - matching on the fly
  - sequential design
  - randomized controlled trial
  - causal inference
abstract: >
  EDI (Experimental Design and Inference) is a library of experimental
  designs, both fixed and sequential, that use matching-on-the-fly
  techniques to maintain covariate balance, paired with inference
  procedures (exact, asymptotic, and distribution-free) tailored to each
  design and response type (continuous, incidence, count, proportion,
  survival, and ordinal). The core model-fitting kernels are written in
  C++ (Eigen + LBFGS++) for speed, with both an R package (EDI, R6-based)
  and a Python package (edi_kernels, pybind11-based) built on the shared
  core.
